        "original_id": "ae5790d1-612f-5163-8f4c-fcc6ab4241a2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Duke Ellington, Billie Holiday, Fred Waller, Lester Young\n- Works: Symphony in Black: A Rhapsody of Negro Life, A Rhapsody of Negro Life\n- Companies: Paramount Pictures\n- Topics: jazz music, pop singing, screen debut, nicknames\n\nFacts:\n- In 1935, Symphony in Black: A Rhapsody of Negro Life was produced as a nine-and-a-half-minute musical short featuring Duke Ellington’s early extended piece A Rhapsody of Negro Life.\n- Symphony in Black: A Rhapsody of Negro Life was directed by Fred Waller and distributed by Paramount Pictures.\n- Symphony in Black: A Rhapsody of Negro Life marked Billie Holiday’s screen debut.\n- Lester Young, Billie Holiday’s friend and music partner, nicknamed her Lady Day.\n- Billie Holiday had a seminal influence on jazz music and pop singing.",
